---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="UtilDock runs entirely in your browser. No document you paste ever leaves your device — there is no server to send it to."
>
  <article class="ud-prose mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4.5vw,3rem)] text-chalk">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div
      class="mt-8 flex items-start gap-3 border border-sound/30 bg-sound/8 p-4 sm:p-5"
    >
      <Icon name="lock" size={19} class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-sound" />
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk">
        <strong class="font-semibold">Nothing you paste into {SITE.name} ever leaves your browser.</strong
        > Every tool is JavaScript running in your own tab. Your JSON never leaves your device, is
        never uploaded, and is never seen by us — there is no server that could receive it. The one
        thing kept between visits is kept <em class="not-italic underline decoration-scribe-strong underline-offset-4"
          >on your machine</em
        >, and is described below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-temper">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-chalk">How the tools work</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          {SITE.name} is a static website. When you open a tool, your browser downloads some HTML,
          CSS and JavaScript, and everything after that happens locally. Parsing, formatting,
          validating and comparing all run inside a Web Worker in your tab. Opening a file with the <strong
            class="font-medium text-chalk">Load</strong
          > button — or dropping one onto the page — reads it from your disk into memory; it is not an
          upload.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-chalk">What is stored on your device</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          So that a refresh does not lose your work, each tool saves its current input to your
          browser's <code class="bg-anvil-lit px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">localStorage</code>,
          along with your theme choice and a few preferences such as indent size. This data stays on
          your device, is readable only by {SITE.name} in your browser, and is never transmitted
          anywhere. Clearing your browser's site data for this domain removes all of it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-chalk">Cookies, tracking and analytics</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          {SITE.name} sets no cookies, runs no advertising, and embeds no third-party trackers,
          social widgets, or hosted fonts. There is no account system, so there is nothing to sign up
          for and no profile to build. You will never see a consent banner here, because there is
          nothing to consent to.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          That includes analytics. There is no analytics script of any kind on this site — not even a
          cookieless one. Hosted analytics products work by loading code from another company's
          servers and reporting back to them, which is exactly the thing this site is built not to
          do. Whatever we know about traffic comes from the web host's own request logs, described
          below; nothing extra runs in your page to produce it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-chalk">Server logs</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The site is served as static files by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare
          processes the network requests needed to deliver a page and may retain limited technical
          data (such as IP address and user agent) for security and abuse prevention, governed by
          Cloudflare's own policies. That applies only to requests for the site's own files — the
          content you paste into a tool is never part of any request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-chalk">Verifying this yourself</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You do not have to take our word for it. Open your browser's developer tools, switch to the
          Network tab, and use any tool on this site: you will see requests for the page's own assets
          and nothing else. Better still, load a tool once and then disconnect from the internet — it
          keeps working, because there was never anything to send.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-chalk">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If this policy ever changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it. The
          commitment that your data stays in your browser is not something we intend to revisit.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
